From: Cherub Kumar <ckumar1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 13:25:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 040/110] feat: per-crew-member theme colors + window tint
 fixes (#3577)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat: support per-crew-member theme colors (gt-zxw)

Add crew_themes config key to ThemeConfig (rig-level) and TownThemeConfig
(town-level) that maps crew member names to theme names. Checked before
role-level fallback in the resolution cascade, so individual crew members
can have distinct colors while others default to the role theme.

Resolution order is now:
  1. Rig crew_themes[member]  (NEW)
  2. Rig role_themes[role]
  3. Rig theme (disabled/custom/named)
  4. Town crew_themes[member]  (NEW)
  5. Town role_defaults[role]
  6. Town theme
  7. Built-in role defaults
  8. Special/auto-assigned

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Executed-By: gastown/crew/woodhouse

* fix: rig-level window_tint should override global role_tints

When a rig has its own window_tint config (even just enabled: true),
it should be the final word. Previously, global role_tints from
mayor/config.json would override rig-level intent — so a rig with
per-member crew_themes would get the global role tint (e.g., teal
for all crew) instead of matching each member's status bar color.

Now: rig window_tint is checked first. If the rig opted in but
provided no specific colors, return nil so the caller inherits from
the per-member status bar theme. Global config only applies when the
rig has no window_tint config at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Executed-By: gastown/crew/woodhouse

* feat: darken window background when inheriting from status bar theme

When window tint inherits from the status bar (no explicit colors
configured), darken the background to 40% brightness so the status
bar stands out visually. Configurable via tint_factor (0.0-1.0) in
the window_tint config at rig or town level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Executed-By: gastown/crew/woodhouse

* fix: resolve window tint on crew start/resume (gt-766)

crew/manager.go resolved the status bar theme but skipped window tint,
so crew sessions started without background tinting. Added the same
ResolveWindowTint + DarkenColor fallback logic that theme.go uses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Executed-By: gastown/crew/woodhouse
